id: pm-olcoon
title: Normalize local parent shorthand consistently with dependency identifiers
description: "Manual packed-CLI testing showed that create --parent parent-a persists the literal dangling reference while --dep id=parent-a normalizes to pm-parent-a. Define an SDK-first identifier contract for parent scalars: either normalize unqualified local identifiers consistently or emit an explicit ambiguity/refusal with an executable canonical retry, without breaking intentional cross-workspace references."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[6]: "area:cli","area:sdk",hierarchy,identifiers,normalization,transport-parity
created_at: "2026-08-21T14:49:23.426Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-05T18:34:24.152Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-05T18:34:23.586Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-05T18:34:23.586Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "A public SDK identifier parser distinguishes canonical local ids, unqualified local shorthand, and explicit cross-workspace references; parent scalars and dependency rows call the same parser across create, update, plan materialization, CLI, MCP, packages, npx and bunx; unambiguous local shorthand normalizes identically or every surface refuses with one typed ambiguity code and an executable canonical retry; intentional remote identifiers remain byte-stable; negative controls cover dangling shorthand, ambiguous prefixes, already-prefixed ids, remote ids, and mixed parent/dependency writes; packed-consumer tests prove no behavior divergence; validation and graph audit report zero new missing hierarchy targets."
goal: canonical local identifiers
objective: Apply one SDK-owned normalization and ambiguity contract to parent scalars and dependency identifiers across every mutation surface
value: "Agents can use short local identifiers safely without creating dangling hierarchy, while cross-workspace references retain explicit meaning"
why_now: "Packed-consumer acceptance reproduced divergent handling between create --parent and --dep, and this is the only active item missing baseline acceptance, risk, confidence, and estimate metadata."
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Added shared public SDK normalization for local parent and dependency references while preserving explicit remote identity.
expected_result: Create/update and delegated hosts persist the same canonical local references and preserve remote case.
actual_result: "Direct SDK and CLI regressions pass; a separately installed packed consumer confirms shorthand parent creation, remote update, and canonical restoration."
